    "commit_sha": "a057663329f34d5f95b11ce1a66bdd33c23cddfc",
    "summary": "The Pantheon review bridge records approve and reopen decisions as COMMENT reviews with proof tags under review_gate.github_review_identity=shared, and the shared verifier in ajoe734/pantheon@dev publishes the Pantheon canonical review gate commit status because review_gate.github_review_bridge_required is true."
  },
  "changes": [
    "docs/conventions/GIT_WORKFLOW.md: updated section 6 table and branch protection description to match the 2026-11-09 gh api read-back of execute-plans dev and main (and upstream pantheon dev and master), stating that execute-plans dev requires four checks bound to the GitHub Actions app (app_id: 15368) including Pantheon canonical review gate (added 2026-11-09T23:36:52Z) with strict: true, a pull-request rule with 0 approvals, and enforce_admins.enabled: false, while execute-plans main does not require Pantheon canonical review gate; updated section 6.1 to document shared identity mode and residual risk (GitHub now refuses a merge into dev without a green gate, a holder of the shared GitHub credential can still deliberately push a proof tag or add the delivery:tooling label, and only a separate review identity closes that).",
    ".github/workflows/pantheon-canonical-review-gate.yml: updated only the header comment to state that Pantheon canonical review gate is a required status check on execute-plans/dev (bound to the GitHub Actions app, app_id: 15368) and not on execute-plans/main, and that the shared Pantheon verifier publishes it while review_gate.github_review_bridge_required is true; every non-comment line stays byte-identical."
  ],
  "unchanged_boundaries": [
